[1m[38;5;231mWhich tooling should I set up from the start? (Nothing is configured today.)[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m [38;5;153mUnit tests (node:test)[39m
  [38;5;246mNode's built-in test runner plus a `npm test` script. Zero dependencies, and the pure core is exactly the kind of code
[39m  [38;5;246mthat pays this back. Strongly recommended.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [ ] Lint + format (ESLint + Prettier)
  [38;5;246mThe JS standard pair. Adds devDependencies and node_modules to a currently zero-dependency repo.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] End-to-end tests
  [38;5;246mBrowser-driven tests (Playwright) over the real form. Heavy for a fixture this size; the DOM layer can be covered more
[39m  [38;5;246mcheaply.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] None — just the code
  [38;5;246mNo test or lint infrastructure. I'd verify by hand and say exactly what I did and didn't check.[39m
